# Every text file is LF in the repository and in every checkout, Windows included.
#
# Without it, `core.autocrlf=true` (Windows' default) checks the sources out as CRLF while the
# generators write LF — or a mix, when they copy a source into their output — so every build on
# Windows showed ~80 generated files as modified, and a shebang ending in `\r` broke a script. Rules
# per path covered each case as it surfaced (the hooks, the .mjs/.cjs scripts, the certification
# scenarios, the UI manifest) and missed the next one; one rule covers them all.
# packages/core/tests/line-endings.test.ts and shebang-eol.test.ts fail when a file escapes it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries are never converted.
*.png binary

# `eol=lf` settles the line TERMINATORS. A `\r\n` sitting INSIDE a JSON string value is content to
# git, not a line ending: the UI manifest's generator normalises it itself (normalizeEol in
# packages/ui/scripts/gen-manifest.mjs).
